refentry.refsect1:
&reftitle.description;
boolstream_is_local resourcestringstream
Checks if a stream, or a URL, is a local one or not.

&reftitle.parameters;




   stream



     The stream resource or URL to check.

&reftitle.returnvalues;
Returns &true; if the stream or URL is local, &false; otherwise.
A stream or URL is local when its wrapper is not flagged as a URL wrapper, so that it is not subject to allow_url_fopen. Plain paths and the file://, php://, glob://, phar:// and compress.* wrappers give &true;, whereas http, https, ftp, ftps, data: and user-space wrappers registered with STREAM_IS_URL give &false;. A scheme that is not registered emits an E_WARNING and gives &true;. Streams that have no wrapper, such as sockets and the pipes of popen and proc_open, give &false;.

&reftitle.changelog;





    &Version;
    &Description;





    8.0.0

     Now throws a TypeError if
     stream is not a valid stream resource.
     Previously, an E_WARNING was raised and &false;
     was returned.

  &reftitle.examples;



    stream_is_local example


     Basic usage example.



<?php
var_dump(stream_is_local("http://example.com"));
var_dump(stream_is_local("/etc"));


    &example.outputs;


bool(false)
bool(true)
